Nonlinear equations
Consider the Nagumo or bistable model: \[
u' = a u (1-u)(u-\alpha),
\]
with \(\alpha=0.2\) and \(a=10\). Implement and solve the model in \(t=0,\ldots,2\) with forward Euler for \(h=10^{-3}\) and various values of \(u(0)\).






Solution






MATLABPython


alpha = 0.2;
a = 10;
f = @(u) a*u.*(1-u).*(u-alpha);
h = 1e-3;
T = 2;
t = 0:h:T;
u = zeros(size(t));
fig = figure; hold on;
for u0 = [0.1,0.2,0.25,0.3,0.6,0.8]
    u(1) = u0;
    for n = 1:length(t)-1
        u(n+1) = u(n) + h*f(u(n));
    end
    plot(t,u,'LineWidth',2.0,'DisplayName',num2str(u0));
end
hold off; grid on; legend;



image





